			<div class="content" id="post-content-4843246">
									

<p><strong>Seeking greenlight:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator pitch:</strong> To save humanity from corruption and wickedness of itself, the seven deadly sins, guidance for humans, were created. However, one individual or entity managed to manifest the sins in our realm inside a book. The ultimate way to cleanse pure humans and irradicate the sinners from corrupting the rest. Anyone willing to read from the book of sinners shall be tested by the sins itself of their purity and corruptness. Those unlucky to fail will have their soul trapped inside the book, and their face, name, and sin burned on the last pages of the book, being held captive for all eternity. If no human voluntarily tests themselves within a day, the book will choose a sinful challenger within a certain radius around it. Unfortunately, to this date, there is no record of anyone passing all the seven sins successfully. The corruption of sins must have spread out of control because a corrupt mind will corrupt its kind.</p>
<p><strong>Central narrative:</strong> The main focus will be around two site researchers assigned to this anomaly. Both of them will get themselves challenged by the sins, with one successfully passing it. The first one being forced by the book to read the first page because within a day, no volunteer was found. The other voluntarily trapping herself inside the book to prevent another human from being randomly selected. Each of the two will give a unique perspective about the realm of the sins, the sins themselves (so to say their representatives), the seven tests, and the ones who failed the trial.<br />
One or two short test logs might be added to demonstrate certain &quot;incidents&quot; regarding this SCP. For example, a researcher is forced by the book to read the first page, after he forced a child to do the same.</p>
<p><strong>Hook, attention grabber:</strong> Interesting to me is to learn about the different trial runs of the two individuals with their backstory, moral thoughts, and purest form.<br />
Add to that the few hints around the price, or let's call it achievement someone would receive if he or she passes all the tests.</p>

